From: "Claude (session)" <claude@session>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 07:23:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] timezone: vlr data-utc-ts is US-Eastern wall time, not
 UTC

Parser now localizes the attribute to America/New_York and converts to
true UTC (DST-aware). One-time marker-guarded migration reinterprets every
stored start_ts (store, upcoming, ledger metadata) the same way, re-sorts
the store across the DST seam, and auto-runs at the top of the refresh
cycle so Render self-heals; scripts/migrate_store_tz.py for the Mac.
Frontend time rendering extracted to time.js: viewer-local with an explicit
zone label, naive strings treated as UTC; node --test suite added (npm
test). LOG entry 29.
